  "dispatch_clarifications": {
    "clarification_i_q3_shift": "For q_3(z_0, z_1) = z_0 z_1 (2 z_0 - 1), q_3(z^(3)) = 1/2, so the nonlinear perturbation b_2(z_A, z_B) + q_3(z_A) u changes b_2 at h_A = 3 by u/2 (not u), and Delta_B(z_A, z_B) + lambda q_3(z_B) changes Delta_B at h_B = 3 by lambda/2.",
    "clarification_ii_sigma_B_scope": "On the common-ready family R_{(c_0, c_1, b_init, B)}, second contact acceptance alpha_B in {0, 1} is already readable from (d, b_0, b_2) without sigma_B because d = C_1(h_B) determines z_B = eta(d): when z_B = 0, Delta_B = 0 in [0, B] is always accepted (alpha_B = 1), and when z_B != 0, R_0 z_B != 0 so b_2 - D_2(R_0^{-1} b_0) = alpha_B R_0 z_B determines alpha_B in {0, 1}. By contrast, sigma_A is required to distinguish accepted zero at Contact A (h_A = 0) from refused h_A in {3, 4} at B = 1/5 on (d, b_0, b_2) or Pi_{class+d}, and sigma_B is separately required for the global reversible involution H_{B,B}^2 = id on Z_B and A_B (preventing the single-shared-sigma sign flip on (0, 1)) and for acceptance readout on the buffer-omitted classical projection Pi_class = (X, W, b)."
  },
